<article class="env-lemma" id="0809">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0809">Lemma <span data-tag="0809">31.33.11</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme. Let $b : X' \to X$ be a blowup of $X$ in a closed subscheme. The pullback $b^{-1}D$ is defined for all effective Cartier divisors $D \subset X$ and pullbacks of meromorphic functions are defined for $b$ (Definitions <a href="/tag/01WV" data-tag="01WV">31.14.12</a> and <a href="/tag/02OT" data-tag="02OT">31.24.4</a>). </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemmas <a href="/tag/0804" data-tag="0804">31.33.2</a> and <a href="/tag/01WS" data-tag="01WS">31.14.2</a> this reduces to the following algebra fact: Let $A$ be a ring, $I \subset A$ an ideal, $a \in I$, and $x \in A$ a nonzerodivisor. Then the image of $x$ in $A[\frac{I}{a}]$ is a nonzerodivisor. Namely, suppose that $x (y/a^ n) = 0$ in $A[\frac{I}{a}]$. Then $a^ mxy = 0$ in $A$ for some $m$. Hence $a^ my = 0$ as $x$ is a nonzerodivisor. Whence $y/a^ n$ is zero in $A[\frac{I}{a}]$ as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>